# ngspice reads the noise summary interval; HSPICE noise is against ground (b855300c, part c).
# What the fix was for, as the ledger has it: `noise1 (out 0) noise iprobe=vin start=1k stop=1M
# dec=10`; clean report.
from: hspice
to: spectre
--- input
t
vin in 0 ac 1
r1 in out 1k
.ac dec 10 1k 1meg
.noise v(out) vin
.end
--- output
// t
simulator lang=spectre insensitive=yes
global 0
sprackOptions1 options temp=25 tnom=25
vin (in 0) vsource mag=1
r1 (in out) resistor r=1k
noise1 (out 0) noise iprobe=vin start=1k stop=1M dec=10
--- report
warning[caveat]: options: hspice assumes other defaults for temp, tnom than spectre does; they are written out
